  "text": "**Alex:** So, have you seen the new art exhibit downtown?  \n**Jordan:** No, I haven\u2019t. Is it worth the trip?  \n**Alex:** I think so. The opening last night was insane.  \n**Jordan:** Really? What\u2019s it called?  \n**Alex:** *The Echoes of Time*. It\u2019s supposed to be really abstract.  \n**Jordan:** Abstract? I don\u2019t usually like that kind of stuff.  \n**Alex:** But it\u2019s not just random shapes. There\u2019s a really strong emotional vibe.  \n**Jordan:** Oh, I see. So it\u2019s more about feeling than form?  \n**Alex:** Exactly. It\u2019s like each piece tells a story without words.  \n**Jordan:** That\u2019s kind of intimidating. I mean, how do you read a painting without labels?  \n**Alex:** It\u2019s not supposed to be easy. It challenges you to look deeper.  \n**Jordan:** I guess I need to give it a try. Maybe I\u2019ll go this weekend.  \n**Alex:** You should. I\u2019ll show you the one piece that really stuck with me.  \n**Jordan:** You\u2019ll show me? That would be cool.  \n**Alex:** Yeah, I\u2019d love to. It\u2019s a bit of a walk from here, though.  \n**Jordan:** No problem. I\u2019d rather walk than sit in a stuffy gallery alone.  \n**Alex:** Fair enough. You\u2019ll regret it, though.  \n**Jordan:** I\u2019ll take my chances.  \n**Alex:** Good. I\u2019ll be waiting by the door at 3.  \n**Jordan:** 3? Not later?  \n**Alex:** Why? You got something else?  \n**Jordan:** No, I just thought maybe you\u2019d say 4.  \n**Alex:** Nah. I\u2019m not staying late.  \n**Jordan:** Okay. See you then.  \n**Alex:** See you.",
